{"id": "EUVD-2026-76412", "enisaUuid": "ba496952-dfae-3c64-8f56-2a07d045779d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/uverbs: Add UVERBS_ATTR_UHW to UVERBS_METHOD_REG_MR\n\nThe original commit missed that three drivers (mthca, irdma, siw) have UHW\ndata associated with reg_mr that cannot be passed through the ioctl. They\nalso assume that the udata cannot be NULL, so failing to pass a valid\nudata can trigger a NULL udata crash in those drivers.\n\nThis never happens in real systems since in rdma-core ibv_cmd_reg_mr_ex()\ndoes not accept a udata and those three drivers don't use it, however a\nmalicious userspace could trigger it.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:43:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:47:57", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/71d5c41ac583df09a7c32199bef7d42de7267d07", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9e71d0f4944ba5641e01db29b3256c963656d671", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/011199f46f44a9fd93a9e5ab5d7fd1328d80e9bf"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89506", "GHSA-pfq2-9rm7-2x65"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "044374d1-abe4-384b-8db2-3e7472967dd2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "4b4ec6d8-bed5-351b-ba36-5e90de839759", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.17"}, {"id": "55d3e7b6-1598-3344-98ad-348ce2265798", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "62e51b51-5f74-3b43-98ab-e79e88d406cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "d639e031-32d0-3955-a60b-5d636cee04b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5b2e45049dc06a876bc6b138218ddeb0814502ef <71d5c41ac583df09a7c32199bef7d42de7267d07"}, {"id": "e31613c3-96a7-3bc3-b916-3ab8f57b1f52", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": 